 "c": [
  {"i":5801,"t":["work"],"s":{},"n":"入社 is taught in the jobs and workplace unit. Business is only a loose association."},
  {"i":5804,"t":["society","business"],"s":{"2":["culture"]},"n":"The private/civilian sense (民間企業, 民間人) fits society and business. The folk sense (民間療法, 民間信仰) belongs with culture."},
  {"i":5831,"t":["people","hobbies"],"n":"An expert or master of something is a people word, and the Meijin titles belong to shogi, go and karuta. It is not a job word."},
  {"i":5835,"t":["society","hobbies"],"n":"This means joining an organisation, a club or insurance (保険に加入). Relationships is a loose fit."},
  {"i":5844,"t":["position","time"],"s":{"2":["science"]},"n":"The main sense is a starting point or beginning (原点に戻る), not a thinking word. The coordinate origin is mathematics."},
  {"i":5904,"t":["media"],"n":"週刊 belongs with magazines and publishing (週刊誌). Calendar is a loose association."}
 ],
 "d": [
  {"i":5803,"keep":[2],"n":"伸びをする (stretching one's body) is common everyday usage and fits a body unit"},
  {"i":5804,"keep":[],"n":"the 'folk' sense (民間療法, 民間伝承) is much less common at this level than 'private/civilian'"},
  {"i":5814,"keep":[2],"n":"track and field (陸上部, 陸上競技) is a very common sense and clearly a sports word"},
  {"i":5823,"keep":[],"n":"red-ink corrections is a minor sense; learners meet 赤字 as 'deficit'"},
  {"i":5844,"keep":[],"n":"coordinate origin is a technical math sense, rare for learners"},
  {"i":5905,"keep":[],"n":"door-to-door selling (外交員) is rare; learners know 外交 as diplomacy"},
  {"i":5909,"keep":[],"n":"winning a lottery is common, but it is not taught in a hobbies unit, so the entry is a poor fit"},
  {"i":5935,"keep":[],"n":"at this level 演習 means practice or drill (演習問題); the military-exercise sense is mostly news vocabulary beyond N3"}
 ]
